ncy: Could explain weight loss but doesn't account for blasts", "Diabetic Ketoacidosis: Glucose normal (99 mg/dL), no metabolic acidosis (HCO3- 22 mEq/L)"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (B symptoms: fever, night sweats, weight loss)", "Pancytopenia with blasts", "Visual acuity decline in non-diabetic context"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.4788643533123028, "posterior": 0.07083039428751423, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Normal creatinine and absence of splenomegaly are inconsistent with chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms (e.g., CML, primary myelofibrosis) in accelerated/blas…"], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.19045741324921134, "posterior": 0.21956368011474958, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The 35% blast count exceeds typical thresholds for ALL (15-20%), but absence of lymphoid morphology and atypical neurological findings (ataxia, visual decline)…"], "evidence_against": ["Visual acuity decline and ataxia are not typical of ALL, reducing its likelihood. These findings could represent paraneoplastic phenomena in AML but don't excl…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.85, "level_role": "family", "