ver chronic myeloproliferative disorders in blast crisis, which typically present with a history of chronic disease and splenomegaly."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute onset with constitutional symptoms and 35% blasts (typically >20% in ALL) support a lymphoid neoplasm over myeloid processes?", "summary": "The 35% blast count exceeds typical thresholds for ALL (15-20%), but absence of lymphoid morphology and atypical neurological findings (ataxia, visual decline) reduce lymphoid process likelihood."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the subacute presentation with constitutional symptoms and 35% blasts align with chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms in blast crisis?", "summary": "Blast crisis of CML/polycythemia vera typically follows chronic phases with splenomegaly; absence of these features makes this less likely but not excluded in the context of rapid transformation."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the patient’s diabetes in follow-up and absence of lymphoid-specific features (e.g., blasts with lymphoid morphology) disfavor a myeloid neoplasm in favor of lymphoid processes?", "summary": "Diabetes history is neutral for this distinction. The absence of lymphoid morphology (e.g., T/B-cell immunophenotype) and atypical neurological features (not typical of ALL) mildly disfavor lymphoid processes."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the patient’s visual acuity decline and ataxia (not typical of ALL) inconsistent with a lymphoid neoplasm?", "summary": "Visual acuity decline and ataxia are not typical of ALL, reducing its likelihood. These findings could represent paraneoplastic phenomena in AML but don't exclude blast crisis."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the patient’s normal serum creatinine (1.1 mg/dL) and absence of splenomegaly inconsistent with chronic myeloproliferative neoplasms?", "summary": "Normal creatinine and absence of splenome